 (UPR) through binding to UPR sensors such as ERN1, which in turn inactivates ERN1 signaling (PubMed:24508390). May also regulate the UPR via the EIF2AK3 UPR sensor (PubMed:24508390). Plays a role in platelet aggregation and activation by agonists such as convulxin, collagen and thrombin (PubMed:15466936)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}